    affiliation: "Cardiovascular and Applied Physiology Laboratory, Florida State University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/FSUcaplab/figure-sweat-sodium-heatmap"
url: "https://github.com/FSUcaplab/figure-sweat-sodium-heatmap"
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-03-18
abstract: >-
  R code to model and visualize estimated sweat sodium loss across dry-bulb
  temperature and relative humidity conditions for passive (1-2 METs) and
  active (3-5 METs) interventions, with a Wet Bulb Globe Temperature contour
  overlaid on each panel. Companion code for the associated review article.
keywords:
  - sweat sodium
  - sodium loss
  - thermoregulation
  - wet bulb globe temperature
  - cardiovascular disease prevention
  - data visualization
